{
    "info": {
        "_postman_id": "6c1f3a52-8d4e-4b7a-9c21-5e0f7d3b9a14",
        "name": "Momentec Proof API",
        "description": "Create custom design proofs and track them.\n\n**Setup (once):** open this collection → **Variables** tab → set `baseUrl` to the Lambda Function URL (no trailing slash) and `apiKey` to the `PROOF_API_KEY` value. Save.\n\nEvery request sends the key as the `x-api-key` header automatically (collection **Authorization** tab).\n\n**Typical flow:**\n1. Send one of the **Create job** requests. The `jobId` is saved for you.\n2. Send **Get job status** every 10–15 seconds. Open the response **Visualize** tab for a progress view.\n3. When `state` is `done` or `needs_review`, send **Download PDF** (or open `pdf.url`).\n\nOr open the **Run: create and wait** folder and click **Run** to do all three automatically.\n\nFull reference: `docs/proof-api.md`.",
        "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
    },
    "auth": {
        "type": "apikey",
        "apikey": [
            {
                "key": "key",
                "value": "x-api-key",
                "type": "string"
            },
            {
                "key": "value",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}",
                "type": "string"
            },
            {
                "key": "in",
                "value": "header",
                "type": "string"
            }
        ]
    },
    "variable": [
        {
            "key": "baseUrl",
            "value": "https://vtileokggwrv5n7hvxbm63ulem0cmlrl.lambda-url.ap-southeast-2.on.aws",
            "type": "string"
        },
        {
            "key": "apiKey",
            "value": "715768cc0e52ba578bd6fd3b50cc2e451c221b723ce64f734c9cd3703378457e",
            "type": "string"
        },
        {
            "key": "jobId",
            "value": "",
            "type": "string"
        },
        {
            "key": "pdfUrl",
            "value": "",
            "type": "string"
        },
        {
            "key": "pollCount",
            "value": "0",
            "type": "string"
        }
    ],
    "event": [
        {
            "listen": "prerequest",
            "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                    "// Catch the two setup mistakes before anything is sent.",
                    "const base = pm.collectionVariables.get(\u0027baseUrl\u0027) || \u0027\u0027;",
                    "const key = pm.collectionVariables.get(\u0027apiKey\u0027) || \u0027\u0027;",
                    "if (base.includes(\u0027YOUR-FUNCTION-URL\u0027)) { throw new Error(\u0027Set the collection variable baseUrl to your Lambda Function URL first.\u0027); }",
                    "if (base.endsWith(\u0027/\u0027)) { pm.collectionVariables.set(\u0027baseUrl\u0027, base.replace(/\\/+$/, \u0027\u0027)); }",
                    "// Requests that inherit the collection auth have no auth of their own; only noauth ones skip the key.",
                    "const usesKey = !(pm.request.auth \u0026\u0026 pm.request.auth.type === \u0027noauth\u0027);",
                    "if (usesKey \u0026\u0026 key.startsWith(\u0027PASTE_\u0027)) { throw new Error(\u0027Set the collection variable apiKey to your PROOF_API_KEY first.\u0027); }"
                ]
            }
        }
    ],
    "item": [
        {
            "name": "Create job",
            "description": "Start a new proof. Each request saves the returned `jobId` into the collection variable so **Get job status** works right after.\n\n`images`: 1–8 items, each an https link (string or `{ \"url\": ... }`) or base64 (plain, `data:` URI, or `{ \"data\": ... }`). Base64 images together ≤ 4 MB; each linked image ≤ 10 MB.\n\n`size`: XS, S, M, L, XL, 2XL, 3XL (default L). `quality`: high (default), medium, low.",
